  "notes": "Compound of {回|かい} (turn, revolve) + {復|ふく} (return). One of the most common words for recovery in Japanese, used for health, economics, systems, and abstract qualities.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {体力|たいりょく}{回復|かいふく}: physical recovery\n- {景気|けいき}{回復|かいふく}: economic recovery\n- {回復|かいふく}の{見込|みこ}み: prospects for recovery\n- {早期|そうき}{回復|かいふく}: early recovery\n- {信頼|しんらい}{回復|かいふく}: restoring trust\n- {名誉|めいよ}{回復|かいふく}: restoration of honor\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive in sense 1 ({景気|けいき}が{回復|かいふく}する). Transitive in sense 2 ({信頼|しんらい}を{回復|かいふく}する).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {治|なお}る: to heal, to get better (everyday, for illness or injuries)\n- {復旧|ふっきゅう}する: to restore (infrastructure, services — after disaster)\n- {復活|ふっかつ}する: to revive, to come back (from complete absence or inactivity)",
